# Money Exchange System

An Object-Oriented Python application integrated with SQLite designed to manage a currency exchange business.

## Project Scope
This system enables exchange businesses to:
* Manage customer profiles and compliance details.
* Maintain a catalog of global currencies.
* Update and track changing exchange rates.
* Process and record secure currency exchange transactions.

---

## Database Architecture & Table Justification

The database consists of **4 core tables** structured to maintain data integrity, reduce redundancy, and ensure compliance.

| Table Name | Description | Justification |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`customers`** | Stores client information (Name, Email, Phone, Legal ID). | **Compliance & Tracking:** Money exchange businesses are legally required to track who is buying/selling currency for auditing and anti-money laundering (AML) purposes. |
| **`currencies`** | Stores supported currency codes, names, and symbols (e.g., USD, EUR). | **Master Data Management:** Ensures consistency across transactions and rates so users cannot input arbitrary or misspelled currency strings. |
| **`exchange_rates`** | Tracks historical and current conversion rates between currency pairs. | **Fluctuation Control:** Exchange rates change constantly. This table acts as a log/registry so transactions can accurately reference the exact rate active at the exact time of trade. |
| **`transactions`** | Records every exchange event (Customer, Source, Target, Amounts, Rate). | **Business Ledger:** Serves as the immutable operational log of the business for accounting, receipts, and reporting. |

---

## How to Run the Project

1. Ensure you have **Python 3.x** installed.
2. Clone the repository and navigate to the project directory.
3. Run the application:
   ```bash
   python main.py

 ER Diagram Design & Database SchemaThe system is designed around four core entities to handle the full scope of a money exchange business:Customer: Stores details about the individuals performing exchanges.Currency: Stores available currencies (e.g., USD, EUR, JPY) and their base units.ExchangeRate: Stores conversion rates relative to a base currency.Transaction: Records the exchange operations, linking customers, source currencies, target currencies, amounts, and rates.Entity-Relationship Structure (Textual ERD)Customer (1) $\leftrightarrow$ ($\infty$) Transaction (A customer can make many transactions)Currency (1) $\leftrightarrow$ ($\infty$) Transaction (As source currency or target currency)Currency (1) $\leftrightarrow$ ($\infty$) ExchangeRate (A currency can have historical/current rates)2. Project File StructurePlaintextmoney_exchange_project/
│
├── database.py       # OOP Database Manager (SQLite)
├── models.py         # OOP Domain Models (Customer, Currency, ExchangeRate, Transaction)
├── main.py           # Application entry point / Demo script
├── requirements.txt  # Project dependencies (optional/standard library)
└── README.md         # Documentation with table justification